invariant: INV-17
file: src/sha3_andn.h
catches: sha3_equiv_test
reason: keccak_f1600_andn_with no longer writes zeros over the scratch
  state, so the state before the last round stays in it after the call.
  Keccak-f[1600] is a permutation, so that state gives back each state
  before it, as far back as the input. The equivalence test hands the
  call a scratch state of its own and requires zeros in it after each
  permutation.

--- old
    keccak_rounds_andn(a, scratch);
    ct_wipe(scratch, 25 * sizeof(uint64_t));
--- new
    keccak_rounds_andn(a, scratch);
